## Individual Progress

### Things that worked well
My teammates completed their work quickly, and we were able to settle on using a few
discord channels to communicate changes and things better than what was seen in iteration 1 (imo).


### Things that could be improved
Because there wasn't that much to do this iteration, there doesn't seem to 
be much to comment on besides my own shortcomings, and issues that should have been caught in the first iteration.
- An area of improvement in our work could be *consistency in formatting*, in both file names and templates i.e. meeting minutes. 
	I feel like a lot of our work follow different templates.
	Not a huge issue, and at this stage of the assignment, this can be easily resolved and I aim to discuss this with my team later.
- Another area of improvement is setting in stone a routine of *quality checking*. This may be a late realization, 
but I've realized that there'll be a lot of work to go through at the final submission date (of course, maybe we could reserve a week before the deadline to do this, but quality checking work at completion is just better practice and a crucial soft skill to have in team project environments), and that perhaps, to ease the workload for the future, we could quality check our work the moment the work is done. I acknowledge that it's a bit dumb to have only realized something like that now, but better late than never. 


Otherwise, I'm happy with my team and hope to support more through the next iteration, hopefully without being too overbearing.

